My sense is that people avoid cumbersome locutions because they are=20
cumbersome, so on the whole you'd only get usage of them if we actually=20
said to the community "In your usage, please don't try too hard to achieve
conciseness -- say what you wish to say ignoring its clunkiness, and then=20
in the light of this we will add to the language zipfean shortenings".

#No doubt, if usage proved such to be the case, then=20
#postbaseline revision would find a few of the lerfu and Mex words that=20
#Jorge despises, being displaced by things that have proven more useful.

This is quite a radical change. Some of those may have been learnt and
used already. I doubt that our conservative constituency would stand
for it.

